The code statements that lead to the bug are:
struct irdma_create_ah_resp uresp;  
...  
uresp.ah_id = ah->sc_ah.ah_info.ah_idx;  
Reason: The `uresp` variable is declared without initialization, so its `rsvd[4]` field contains uninitialized kernel stack data. Only `ah_id` is assigned before `ib_copy_to_udata()` copies the entire structure (including the uninitialized `rsvd` bytes) to user space, resulting in a 4-byte kernel stack leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
struct irdma_create_ah_resp uresp = {};  
Reason: Changing the declaration to `= {}` zero-initializes all fields of `uresp`, including `rsvd[4]`. This ensures no uninitialized stack data is copied to user space, fixing the information leak.

